# Router & API

## apiRequest

```javascript
import { apiRequest } from "../services/api";
import { HttpMethods, Endpoints } from "../constants";

const response = await apiRequest(HttpMethods.GET, Endpoints.GET_USER_PROFILE);
if (response?.status === HttpStatus.OK) {
  globalStore.setUser(response.data.data);
}
```

- reCAPTCHA auto-attached on POST/PUT/PATCH (except `Endpoints.ALIVE`)
- FormData: append `captchaResponse` manually for multipart

## Router guards (`router/index.js`)

- Fetch countries before auth when needed
- `POST Endpoints.ALIVE` validates session
- 401 → clear token, redirect to Auth
- OAuth: only allow callback when `globalStore.redirect[action].redirectPending`

## New routes

1. Add to `ApplicationRoutes` + `ApplicationRouteNames`
2. Register in `routes` array
3. Extend `beforeEach` if auth rules differ from default
4. Use `router.push({ name: ApplicationRouteNames.X })`

## New endpoints

1. `Endpoints.MY_ACTION = "/path"` (match API `/api` prefix if base URL excludes it — follow existing pattern)
2. Whitelist in `.env` if public (no Bearer token)
